### Article 13

Powers of free legal aid centres in the field of preventing and combating domestic violence
{Title of Article 13 as amended by Law No. 3022-IX of 10.04.2023}
1. The powers of free legal aid centres in the field of preventing and combating domestic violence include:
{First paragraph of part one of Article 13 as amended by Law No. 3022-IX of 10.04.2023}
1) ensuring the provision of free legal aid to victims in the manner established by the Law of Ukraine "On Free Legal Aid", including on the basis of general and special support services for victims;
{Second paragraph of part one of Article 13 as amended by Law No. 3022-IX of 10.04.2023}
2) interaction with other subjects implementing measures in the field of preventing and combating domestic violence, in accordance with Article 15 of this Law;
3) reporting to the central executive authority implementing state policy in the field of preventing and combating domestic violence on the results of exercising powers in this field in the manner determined by the central executive authority ensuring the formation of state policy in the field of preventing and combating domestic violence.

### Article 14

Powers of general and specialized support services for victims
1. General and specialized support services for victims within their powers carry out:
1) reception and consideration of applications from victims or their representatives for receiving assistance, including social services for persons in difficult life circumstances;
2) informing local state administrations, local self-government bodies, authorized units of the National Police of Ukraine about the detection of facts of domestic violence with the voluntary informed consent of victims, except in cases of violence against children and incapacitated persons or detection of acts of violence of a criminal nature, when such consent is not required; in case of detection of a fact of domestic violence against a child - informing no later than one day the children's affairs service and authorized units of the National Police of Ukraine;
3) assessment of the needs of victims;
4) providing victims with full and comprehensive information about their rights and opportunities to receive effective assistance;
5) providing victims, in accordance with competence, with social services, medical, social, psychological assistance on a free basis, facilitating the provision of legal aid, as well as ensuring temporary shelter for such persons and their children in the manner provided by law;
{Point 5 of part one of Article 14 as amended by Law No. 3022-IX of 10.04.2023}
6) informing, in the manner established by law, local state administrations and local self-government bodies about persons who received assistance and about the results of its provision.
2. Specialized support services for victims (except the call centre on preventing and combating domestic violence, gender-based violence and violence against children) are established by local executive authorities and local self-government bodies in accordance with the law and operate on the basis of model regulations on specialized support services for victims approved by the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine.
{Resolutions of the CMU No. 654, No. 655, No. 824}
The call centre on preventing and combating domestic violence, gender-based violence and violence against children is established by the central executive authority ensuring the formation of state policy in the field of preventing and combating domestic violence, belongs to the sphere of its management and operates on the basis of a regulation approved by this authority. The call centre on preventing and combating domestic violence, gender-based violence and violence against children is a state institution having territorial branches in all regions of Ukraine.
3. Specialized support services for victims function in the manner established by law at the expense of state and local budgets, funds of enterprises, institutions, organizations, trade unions, voluntary contributions of legal entities and individuals, other sources not prohibited by law.
4. Issues regarding the stay of victims in specialized support services for such persons and the provision of social services to them are regulated by the constituent documents of the said services in accordance with the standards for the provision of social services to victims, which are approved by the central executive authority ensuring the formation of state policy in the field of preventing and combating domestic violence, taking into account the requirements of international legal acts.

