### Article 16

Unified State Register of Cases of Domestic Violence and Gender-Based Violence
1. The Unified State Register of Cases of Domestic Violence and Gender-Based Violence (hereinafter - the Register) is an automated information and communication system designed for the collection, registration, accumulation, storage, adaptation, modification, renewal, use, dissemination (distribution, implementation, transfer), depersonalization and destruction of data determined by this Law on cases of domestic violence and gender-based violence.
{Part one of Article 16 as amended in accordance with Law No. 2801-IX of 01.12.2022}
1) protection of vital interests of victims, including child victims;
2) prevention of repeated cases of domestic violence and gender-based violence;
3) ensuring the implementation of measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of domestic violence and in the field of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence;
4) provision of comprehensive and timely assistance to victims by entities implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of domestic violence and in the field of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence;
5) recording of cases of domestic violence and gender-based violence;
6) coordination of activities of entities implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of domestic violence and in the field of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence.
3. The Register shall contain information (separately for each case of violence) on:
1) the employee of an entity implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of domestic violence, or an entity implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence, who entered information on a case of violence into the Register or corrected it (date of entry; surname, first name, patronymic; position; contact telephone number; name and address of the relevant entity);
2) the person who reported the commission of violence (surname, first name, patronymic; day, month, year of birth; place of residence; contact telephone number) - with consent provided in the manner determined by part four of this Article;
3) the victim (surname, first name, patronymic; day, month, year of birth; sex; citizenship; place of residence; place of study and/or place of work; contact telephone number) - with consent provided in the manner determined by part four of this Article;
4) the offender (surname, first name, patronymic; day, month, year of birth; sex; citizenship; place of residence; place of study and/or place of work; contact telephone number) and on the nature of the relationship between the offender and the victim, including in accordance with Article 3 of this Law;
5) the case of domestic violence, gender-based violence (date of commission; place of commission; form of domestic violence; type of harm or suffering inflicted as a result of gender-based violence; brief description);
6) the needs of the victim;
7) entities implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of domestic violence, or entities implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence, in connection with the detection of a case of violence (name; powers; location and contact telephone number (except for specialized support services);
8) an exhaustive list of measures implemented in connection with the detection of a case of violence, and their result.
4. Consent to the entry of personal data on the person who reported the commission of violence, or on the victim, is provided by the relevant person in compliance with the requirements of the Law of Ukraine "On Protection of Personal Data".
In the event that the specified person is a child, such consent is provided by their parents or other legal representatives, and if the parents (other legal representatives of the child) are offenders or evade the protection of the rights and interests of the child - by the guardianship and trusteeship authority. In the event that the specified person is incapacitated, such consent is provided by their legal representative, and if their legal representative is an offender or evades the protection of the rights and interests of the incapacitated person - by the guardianship and trusteeship authority.
5. Personal data on the person who reported the commission of violence shall be stored in the Register for one year from the date of receipt of the relevant information on the commission of violence.
Personal data on the victim shall be stored in the Register for three years from the date of commission of domestic violence or gender-based violence.
Personal data on the offender shall be stored in the Register:
1) in the absence of criminal proceedings against the offender in connection with the commission of domestic violence, gender-based violence or other forms of violence against the victim, a court decision on the application of a restrictive order or imposition of an administrative penalty, a court verdict on finding the offender guilty of committing domestic violence or gender-based violence or other forms of violence against the victim, that have entered into legal force - for one year from the date of receipt of the relevant information on the commission of violence;
2) in the event of an acquittal verdict of the court that has entered into legal force - until the entry into force of the relevant court decision;
3) in the event of initiation of criminal proceedings against the offender in connection with the commission of domestic violence or gender-based violence or other forms of violence against the victim - for the period of investigation of the criminal proceedings;
4) in the event of adoption of a court decision that has entered into legal force on the application of a restrictive order or imposition of an administrative penalty - for three years from the date of entry into force of the relevant court decision;
5) in the event of issuance of a court verdict that has entered into legal force on finding the offender guilty of committing domestic violence or gender-based violence or other forms of violence against the victim with serving of punishment - for ten years from the date of expiration of the term of serving the punishment;
6) in the event of issuance of a court verdict that has entered into legal force on finding the offender guilty of committing domestic violence or gender-based violence or other forms of violence against the victim without serving of punishment - for ten years from the date of entry into force of the relevant court decision.
In the event of refutation of the fact of commission of violence, as well as after the expiration of the storage period in the Register of personal data, such data shall be subject to deletion or destruction in the manner established by law.
6. Formation of the Register is carried out separately for each case of domestic violence, gender-based violence by entering the relevant information into it.
Information into the Register (except for information on the offender) is entered by all entities implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of domestic violence, or entities implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence (except for citizens of Ukraine, foreigners and stateless persons who are in Ukraine on legal grounds).
Information on the offender is entered into the Register by:
1) responsible structural subdivisions of local state administrations, whose powers include the implementation of measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of domestic violence or in the field of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence;
2) responsible executive bodies of village, settlement, city, district in cities (in case of their creation) councils, whose powers include the implementation of measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of domestic violence or in the field of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence;
3) authorized subdivisions of bodies of the National Police of Ukraine.
Information on the offender is entered into the Register in the event of a reasonable suspicion of their commission of violence, in particular after confirmation of such fact by conducting a verification of the relevant information in accordance with the procedure for interaction of entities implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of domestic violence, and/or the procedure for interaction of entities implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence, approved by the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine.
7. Access to the Register is granted to:
1) employees of specially authorized bodies in the field of prevention and counteraction of domestic violence, the specially authorized central executive body on issues of ensuring equal rights and opportunities for women and men, whose official duties include prevention and counteraction of domestic violence, gender-based violence;
2) authorized persons (coordinators) on issues of ensuring equal rights and opportunities for women and men, prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence of local state administrations and village, settlement, city, district in cities (in case of their creation) councils;
3) employees of responsible structural subdivisions of local state administrations and responsible executive bodies of village, settlement, city, district in cities (in case of their creation) councils on issues of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence;
4) employees of authorized subdivisions of bodies of the National Police of Ukraine;
5) employees of children's services - in respect of cases of violence in which offenders or victims are children.
Access of relevant employees to the Register is carried out using a qualified electronic signature or an advanced electronic signature based on a qualified certificate of electronic signature and compatible with the software of the Register, or using electronic identification means with a medium or high level of trust in accordance with the requirements of the Law of Ukraine "On Electronic Identification and Electronic Trust Services".
{Paragraph seven of part seven of Article 16 as amended by Law No. 2801-IX of 01.12.2022}
8. The holder of the Register is the central executive body that implements state policy in the field of prevention and counteraction of domestic violence.
9. The administrator of the Register is a state enterprise, determined by the central executive body that implements state policy in the field of prevention and counteraction of domestic violence, belonging to the sphere of its management, implements measures for the creation, implementation and support of the software of the Register, is responsible for its technical and technological support, preservation and protection of data of the Register, implements technical and technological measures for granting, blocking and revoking access to the Register, organizes and conducts training on working with the Register.
10. The totality of information on natural persons (personal data) contained in the Register is information with restricted access. Processing of this information is carried out in compliance with the requirements of the Law of Ukraine "On Protection of Personal Data".
11. The procedure for formation, maintenance and access to the Register is determined by the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine.

