### Article 350

8. Service of the court decision, notification of the issuance or extension of a restrictive order
1. Copies of the full court decision are served to the participants in the case who were present at the court hearing immediately after the announcement of such decision. For participants in the case who were not present at the court hearing, a copy of the court decision is sent by registered mail with acknowledgment of receipt immediately, but no later than the next day from the day of the decision.
2. Regarding the issuance or extension of a restrictive order, the court no later than the next day from the day of the decision notifies the authorized units of the National Police of Ukraine at the place of residence (stay) of the applicant for placing the person in respect of whom a restrictive order has been issued or extended on preventive record, as well as district, district in the cities of Kyiv and Sevastopol state administrations and executive bodies of village, settlement, city, district in cities councils at the place of residence (stay) of the applicant";
