### Article 13

2. Powers of general and specialized support services for victims
General and specialized support services for victims, within their powers, carry out:
reception and consideration of applications from victims or their representatives for assistance, including social services for persons in difficult life circumstances;
informing executive authorities and local self-government bodies about the detection of a fact of gender-based violence with the voluntary informed consent of victims, except in cases of violence against children and incapacitated persons or detection of acts of violence of a criminal nature, when such consent is not required; in case of detection of a fact of gender-based violence against children - informing no later than one day the children's affairs service and authorized units of the National Police of Ukraine;
assessment of the needs of victims;
providing victims with full and comprehensive information about their rights and opportunities to receive effective assistance;
providing victims, in accordance with competence, with social services, medical, social, psychological assistance free of charge, facilitating the provision of legal assistance, as well as ensuring temporary shelter for such persons and their children in the manner prescribed by law;
informing, in the manner established by law, local state administrations and local self-government bodies about persons who received assistance and about the results of its provision.
Specialized support services for victims (except for the call center on prevention and counteraction to domestic violence, gender-based violence and violence against children) are established by local executive authorities and local self-government bodies in accordance with the law and operate on the basis of standard regulations on specialized support services for victims, approved by the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine.
The call center on prevention and counteraction to domestic violence, gender-based violence and violence against children is established by the central executive authority that ensures the formation of state policy in the field of prevention and counteraction to domestic violence, belongs to the sphere of its management and operates on the basis of regulations approved by this authority.
The call center on prevention and counteraction to domestic violence, gender-based violence and violence against children is a state institution that has territorial branches in all regions of Ukraine";
