PREVENTION AND COUNTERACTION TO GENDER-BASED VIOLENCE

### Article 21

2. Prevention of gender-based violence
Measures for the prevention of gender-based violence are carried out in the following directions:
studying the situation and collecting data on facts of gender-based violence;
conducting sectoral and intersectoral research on the state, causes and preconditions for the spread of gender-based violence, as well as the effectiveness of legislation in the field of prevention and counteraction to such violence, the practice of its application;
conducting information campaigns on manifestations of gender-based violence, its consequences, including for children;
conducting information and educational activities in educational institutions on prevention and counteraction to gender-based violence, including against children;
involving mass media in conducting educational campaigns aimed at fulfilling tasks in the field of prevention and counteraction to gender-based violence;
organizing and conducting joint and specialized trainings and seminars for specialists working in the field of prevention and counteraction to gender-based violence, as well as for law enforcement officers and judges;
organizing and implementing programs for persons who have committed gender-based violence, including sexual violence, in the manner established by law.
Entities implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction to gender-based violence take into account its disproportionate impact on women and men, including persons with disabilities, pregnant women, incapacitated persons, elderly persons, the need to support and protect persons who have suffered from gender-based violence, as well as the consequences of such violence that lead to violations of human rights and discrimination on the basis of sex.
The implementation of any measures in the field of prevention of gender-based violence is carried out without discrimination on any grounds.
Citizens of Ukraine, foreigners and stateless persons who are in Ukraine on legal grounds, who become aware of the commission of gender-based violence, are obliged to immediately report this to local state administrations, local self-government bodies, authorized units of the National Police of Ukraine or to the call center on prevention and counteraction to domestic violence, gender-based violence and violence against children.


