The procedure for interaction of entities implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence is approved by the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine.
Entities implementing measures in the field of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence report to the specially authorized central executive body on ensuring equal rights and opportunities for women and men on the results of exercising powers in the field of prevention and counteraction of gender-based violence in the manner determined by the specially authorized central executive body on ensuring equal rights and opportunities for women and men.

### Стаття 21

8. Implementation of programs for perpetrators
The entities responsible for implementation of programs for perpetrators are local state administrations and local self-government bodies.
The entity responsible for implementation of programs for perpetrators organizes and ensures the completion of such programs by perpetrators.
Implementation of programs for perpetrators with respect to child perpetrators is carried out taking into account the age and psychological characteristics of children.
In order to prevent repeated commission of gender-based violence and ensure implementation of the program for the perpetrator, a child perpetrator may be temporarily placed with relatives, in the family of a foster educator or in an institution for children regardless of form of ownership and subordination, in which appropriate conditions for residence, upbringing, education and rehabilitation of the child are created in accordance with their needs.
Implementation of programs for perpetrators is ensured by specialists who have undergone appropriate training.
A perpetrator may be referred by a court to complete a program for perpetrators for a period from three months to one year in cases provided by law.
A perpetrator must have the opportunity to attend a program for perpetrators on their own initiative on a voluntary basis.
In case of failure of a perpetrator to appear for completion of a program for perpetrators or evasion from completing the program without valid reasons, the entities responsible for implementation of programs for perpetrators provide within three working days written notification thereof to the authorized unit of the National Police of Ukraine for taking appropriate measures.
Bringing a perpetrator to liability for failure to complete a program for perpetrators does not release them from the obligation to complete such program.
In case of bringing a perpetrator, including a child perpetrator, to criminal liability, the court may impose on them the obligation to complete a probation program in accordance with paragraph 4 of part two of Article 76 of the Criminal Code of Ukraine";
